    <!--
      Changeset 10: Stored procedure error handling — EXIT HANDLER FOR SQLEXCEPTION
      (items #71-#79).
      Every stored procedure now declares an EXIT HANDLER FOR SQLEXCEPTION that:
        - ROLLBACKs the active transaction (where a transaction is open), and
        - DROPs any session-scoped temporary tables (cleanup on error), and
        - RESIGNALs the original SQL exception to the caller.
      This ensures that errors surface visibly rather than being swallowed, and
      that partial writes cannot persist after an unexpected failure.

      Files in this changeset (one DROP+CREATE per file):
        - sp_events__publish_v2       (item #71)
        - sp_events__publish_advanced_v2  (item #72)
        - sp_events__publish_multi_v3 (item #73)
        - sp_sequence_v3              (item #74)
        - sp_sequence_loop_v3         (item #75)
        - sp_consumers__gc_v3         (item #76)
